.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a source string into a destination buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "../include/mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrcpy
copies the string pointed to by
.I src
into the character buffer pointed to by
.I dest
including the terminating null character.
.PP
The destination buffer must be large enough to hold the source string and its terminating null character.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters copied, excluding the terminating null character.
